      '<b>1. Intake:</b> the intake valve is open, the piston moves down and <b>blue particles of fresh mixture</b> flow through the intake port past the open valve into the cylinder; there are more of them with every millimeter of stroke. <b>2. Compression:</b> the valves are closed, the piston compresses the charge from 549.6 cm³ to 50.05 cm³ (<b>compression ratio 11 : 1</b>) – the cloud of particles gets denser and the blue turns to violet.',
      '<b>3. Power (expansion):</b> the spark plug ignites the mixture <b>before top dead center</b> (spark advance 10° at idle up to 30° at full load): a flash at the plug, and from it the <b>flame front</b> (yellow) spreads, with the orange burning charge behind it. The pressure pushes the piston down and the particles darken to red. <b>4. Exhaust:</b> the exhaust valve opens before bottom dead center – first a fast <b>pressurized blow-down</b>, then the piston pushes the <b>light-brown exhaust gas</b> out through the exhaust port to the left. Around top dead center both valves are briefly open (<b>overlap</b>).',
